</surname><given-names>WA</given-names></name><name><surname>Offit</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name></person-group><source>Vaccines</source><publisher-loc>New York</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Saunders</publisher-name><fpage>1095</fpage><lpage>1176</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="ppat-0030075-b030"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bae</surname><given-names>HG</given-names></name><name><surname>Drosten</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Emmerich</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Colebunders</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Hantson</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Analysis of two imported cases of yellow fever infection from Ivory Coast and The Gambia to Germany and Belgium</article-title><source>J Clin Virol</source><volume>33</volume><fpage>274</fpage><lpage>280</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16036176</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat-0030075-b031"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Swofford</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><source>PAUP&#x0002a;. Phylogenetic analysis using parsimony (&#x0002a; and other methods)</source><publisher-loc>Sunderland (Massachusetts)</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Sinauer Associates</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="ppat-0030075-b032"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Huelsenbeck</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>MRBAYES: Bayesian inference of phylogenetic trees</article-title><source>Bioinformatics</source><volume>17</volume><fpage>754</fpage><lpage>755</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11524383</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat-0030075-b033"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-t